    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Upload your CSV file by pressing the + button next to “Files” and choosing “Upload”\r\n2. In Python, open your data file and read it into a list of rows with the `csv` module’s `DictReader`.\r\n3. Convert the data into a feature matrix of `inputs` and a list of `outputs`. The feature matrix of `inputs` should be a list where each input entry is a list of features you want to use (converted to numbers). Each entry in the `outputs` list should be the value you want your neural network to predict.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nOnce you’ve opened a file and imported the `csv` module, recall that you can read the data from the file into a list with `list(csv.DictReader(file))`. For example, you might use code like:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport csv\r\n\r\nfile = open(\"FILENAME.csv\")\r\nrows = list(csv.DictReader(file))\r\nfile.close()\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo construct a list derived from that data, recall that you can use a list comprehension like `[X for row in rows]`, where `rows` is your list of rows and `X` is a value that uses information from a particular `row`.\r\n\r\nYou can use the `int` and `float` functions to convert strings from your CSV file into numbers.\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor for help if you get stuck!\r\n",
